data.content:
## What Breaks in .NET 11

**Sync I/O via the Cosmos DB provider is fully removed.** In .NET 10 you could opt in to sync-over-async, but in EF Core 11 that opt-in no longer exists. All synchronous calls (`ToList()`, `First()`, `Count()`, `SaveChanges()`) **always throw** — no configuration can restore the old behavior.

### Fix: Convert to async

```csharp
public class ProductRepository
{
    private readonly CosmosDbContext _context;

    public async Task<List<Product>> GetAllAsync()
    {
        return await _context.Products.ToListAsync();
    }

    public async Task<Product> GetByIdAsync(int id)
    {
        return await _context.Products.FirstAsync(p => p.Id == id);
    }

    public async Task<int> GetCountAsync()
    {
        return await _context.Products.CountAsync();
    }

    public async Task SaveAsync(Product product)
    {
        _context.Products.Add(product);
        await _context.SaveChangesAsync();
    }
}
```

This is a **medium-impact** breaking change with no workaround — the entire call chain up to your controllers/handlers must become `async`/`await`. Tracking issue: [dotnet/efcore#37059](https://github.com/dotnet/efcore/issues/37059).
